<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
    <title>H-max</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/style.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/details.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/images/lg.png" type="image/x-icon">
  </head>
  <body>
    <section class="project-detail">
      <div class="container">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a>
        <h1>H-max – Interactive AI Assistant</h1>

        <img src="/images/h-max.png" alt="Hassistante" class="project-banner" />

        <p class="description">
          <strong>H-max</strong> is an AI-based virtual assistant application. It enables interactive and smooth conversations, currently in Beta version. 
          The project focuses on providing helpful responses, an intuitive interface, and a foundation for future AI enhancements.
        </p>

        <h2>Main Features:</h2>
        <ul class="features">
          <li>💬 Intelligent and conversational responses</li>
          <li>📱 Simple and modern user interface</li>
          <li>🌦️ Integrated weather API for real-time weather reports</li>
          <li>🧠 Algorithmic request processing</li>
          <li>🧪 Features under active improvement</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Technologies Used:</h2>
        <ul class="tech-stack">
          <li>⚛️ React</li>
          <li>⚡ Vite.js</li>
          <li>📘 TypeScript</li>
          <li>🔢 Custom algorithmic logic</li>
          <li>🌐 OpenWeatherMap API (Free tier)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Challenges Faced:</h2>
        <ul class="challenges">
          <li>🧩 Designing a lightweight AI logic without relying on heavy external APIs</li>
          <li>🔄 Managing state efficiently for multi-step conversations</li>
          <li>🧪 Ensuring flexibility for future NLP and machine learning integration</li>
          <li>🎨 Keeping the UI clean while adding more features</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Solutions Implemented:</h2>
        <ul class="solutions">
          <li>✅ Built a custom logic layer to simulate intelligent behavior</li>
          <li>✅ Integrated OpenWeatherMap API for dynamic weather reports</li>
          <li>✅ Used React hooks and component-based architecture for modular and scalable design</li>
          <li>✅ Structured the codebase to allow seamless integration of AI models in the future</li>
          <li>✅ Designed with user experience in mind, prioritizing clarity and responsiveness</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Conclusion:</h2>
        <p>
          H-max marks a meaningful step towards building a personalized virtual assistant. 
          Although still in Beta, the system lays a strong foundation for real-time help, automation, and integration with future AI enhancements.
        </p>

        <h2>Future Improvements:</h2>
        <ul class="future">
          <li>📡 Integration with NLP libraries or LLMs for deeper understanding</li>
          <li>💾 Persistent memory to remember user preferences</li>
          <li>📈 Analytics dashboard for user interaction statistics</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://H-max.netlify.app/" target="_blank">🌐 View Demo</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/Hassyunity/assistantante_ia" target="_blank">🔗 View Code</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </body>
</html>
